# Planning artefacts are ignored by default: this directory accumulates
# experiment caches (grid_cache_pt18_*, grid_cache_smooth, ...) worth tens of MB
# of debug pickles and per-point solver logs, none of which belong in git.
*
!.gitignore
!.gitkeep

# The exception is the canonical grid_cache's actual deliverables. The 20 plan
# pickles are 10 MB of the cache's 46 MB and are the trajectories that were
# replayed on the robot, so committing them alongside the change that produced
# them makes every trajectory regression visible in `git status` and bisectable.
# The _debug pickles, the .log files and the .log.gcp1.live streams are the
# other 36 MB and stay ignored -- they are diagnostics for one run, not results.
#
# The event log is committed too. Unlike the per-point .log diagnostics, the log
# IS the result for anything quoted as a runtime number, and every figure in
# timing_report.py is re-derivable from it without replanning. 7 MB of JSONL that
# zlib-compresses to about a tenth of that in the pack.
#
# There is exactly one cache. Measurement runs used to land in sibling
# directories (grid_cache_seq, grid_cache_timing, ...), which meant the answer to
# "which run are these numbers from" depended on a directory name rather than on
# the history -- and two of those siblings were half-finished runs that read as
# results. A new run replaces this one in a commit; the previous run stays
# reachable at the commit that held it.
!grid_cache/
grid_cache/*
!grid_cache/point_[0-9][0-9].pkl
!grid_cache/status.json
!grid_cache/grid_status.png
!grid_cache/timing/
!grid_cache/timing/*.jsonl
